---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Guide"
	description="Get started with Quester Studio — open the sample workspace and run demo-main-nodes."
>
	<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Guide</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
			A short path from first launch to a successful run.
		</p>

		<ol class="mt-8 space-y-6">
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">1. Install Quester Studio</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					<a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-foreground" href={`${base}download/`}
						>Download</a
					>
					an unsigned Windows or Linux build from GitHub Releases and launch the app.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">2. Open the sample workspace</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					On the welcome screen choose <strong class="text-foreground">Open sample</strong>. That loads the
					bundled example with environments and flows.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">3. Select demo-main-nodes</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					In the Flows sidebar open <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1">demo-main-nodes</code>. The canvas
					shows start → input → http → extract → output, with assert on the HTTP response. A disconnected
					<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1">note</code> sticky is for documentation only (not executed).
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">4. Pick env and run</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					Choose environment <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1">local</code> (DummyJSON base URL) and run
					the flow. Watch nodes light up as they execute.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">5. Inspect the result</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					Open the inspector on the http or extract node, then check the run / response panel for status
					and body.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">6. Edit and save</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					Change a label or URL in the inspector and save — the
					<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1">*.flow.json</code> file updates on disk.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li class="grid gap-1">
				<h2 class="text-base font-semibold">7. Go deeper</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
					<a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-foreground" href={`${base}docs/ui/`}
						>UI reference</a
					>
					for screenshots;
					<a class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-foreground" href={`${base}docs/`}
						>Docs</a
					>
					for CLI, workspace, and nodes.
				</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
